    "Captured signals give you the raw material (e.g., 'Users gave this answer a thumbs down'),",
    "While computed signals help you interpret it (e.g., 'The thumbs down was likely due to hallucination, not just poor tone').",
    "Without both, your evaluation would be either too noisy (just raw data) or too abstract (just opinions without context).",
    "The course emphasizes that these signals aren’t unique to chatbots—they’re part of any software evaluation.",
    "The twist with LLMs is that the computed signals (like hallucination or bias) are more nuanced and require specialized tools or models to measure accurately.",
